1.4. "Modified Version" means a copy or adaptation containing changes to protected expression in the Software, other than Permitted Packaging Changes. A work independently created without copying protected expression is not a Modified Version merely because it has similar features, behavior, or compatible interfaces.

1.5. "Permitted Packaging Changes" means changes strictly necessary for building, packaging, installing, signing, or distributing an otherwise unmodified version on a supported or target platform, as described in Section 4.3.

1.6. "Public Distribution" means reproducing or making copies of the Software available to the public or any generally accessible group, including via code-hosting platforms, application stores, download sites, package repositories, or physical media. Development Forks and patches permitted under Section 5 are excluded from the prohibition on Public Distribution of Modified Versions, subject to Section 5's conditions.

1.7. "Development Fork" means a copy or branch made available primarily for development, review, testing, research, or contributing to the official project, and not operated, packaged, or promoted as an independent end-user release.

1.8. "Independent Extension" means independently created plugins, themes, adapters, integrations, companion software, and similar works that interoperate with the Software without incorporating its protected expression beyond what is independently authorized.

1.9. "Monetization" has the meaning stated in Section 7.

1.10. "Third-Party Materials" means code, content, services, or other materials whose rights are held by third parties and which are governed by separate legal rights or license terms.

